WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.853
I know that Little Joe meant to do his best for me after my exhausting run for the doctor.

2
00:00:07.854 --> 00:00:15.216
But he hadn't been working at the stable long and didn't know much yet.

3
00:00:15.217 --> 00:00:20.917
When he brought me into my stall, I was dripping with sweat.

4
00:00:20.918 --> 00:00:26.077
He rubbed my legs and chest but didn't put anything over me to keep me warm.

5
00:00:26.078 --> 00:00:29.866
He thought I was so warm already that I wouldn't like it.

6
00:00:29.867 --> 00:00:32.421
Then he brought me lots of cold water.

7
00:00:32.422 --> 00:00:37.519
It tasted good when I was hot, so I gulped it all down.

8
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.921
Little Joe thought I must be hungry after working so hard.

9
00:00:40.922 --> 00:00:44.537
He brought me a bucket of corn.

10
00:00:44.538 --> 00:00:49.668
Not long after that, I began to tremble and feel very cold.

11
00:00:49.669 --> 00:00:58.175
My legs and chest ached. My stomach felt tight. I was sore all over.

12
00:00:58.176 --> 00:01:00.880
Little Joe had left by then.

13
00:01:00.881 --> 00:01:05.338
I stood there for a long time, wishing I wasn't so cold.

14
00:01:05.339 --> 00:01:09.983
Finally I collapsed onto the straw and tried to sleep.

15
00:01:09.984 --> 00:01:12.880
I woke up when I heard John at the door.

16
00:01:12.881 --> 00:01:18.020
He'd finally finished his long walk home and had come to check on me.

17
00:01:18.021 --> 00:01:23.520
I let out a moan of distress. John was at my side in an instant.

18
00:01:23.521 --> 00:01:29.314
"Oh, Beauty," he exclaimed. "What has that stupid boy done?"

19
00:01:29.315 --> 00:01:33.297
I couldn't tell him how bad I felt, but he seemed to know.

20
00:01:33.298 --> 00:01:36.277
He grabbed a blanket and draped it over me.

21
00:01:36.278 --> 00:01:38.673
Then he brought me some warm food.

22
00:01:38.675 --> 00:01:44.843
I felt a little better after I finished it, and I fell asleep.

23
00:01:44.844 --> 00:01:47.770
The next day I was still very sick.

24
00:01:47.771 --> 00:01:51.743
I had a fever and couldn't breathe without pain.

25
00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:57.632
John stayed by my side, and the squire came to my stall to see me several times.

26
00:01:57.633 --> 00:02:03.902
"My poor Beauty," he said. "You saved your mistress' life, do you know that?

27
00:02:03.903 --> 00:02:08.982
If it had taken the doctor any longer to get here, it would have been too late."

28
00:02:08.983 --> 00:02:13.605
"There was no chance of arriving too late with Beauty," John said.

29
00:02:13.606 --> 00:02:19.412
"I never saw a horse go so fast! It seemed as if he knew what was wrong!"

30
00:02:19.413 --> 00:02:23.202
Of course I knew, even if John didn't realize it.

31
00:02:23.203 --> 00:02:25.943
Maybe I didn't understand everything.

32
00:02:25.944 --> 00:02:33.955
But I understood that I had to go fast, and that it was for the sake of the mistress.

33
00:02:33.956 --> 00:02:41.004
I'm not sure how many days passed while I was sick. The vet came every day.

34
00:02:41.005 --> 00:02:46.927
John moved Ginger and Merrylegs into another part of the stable so I wouldn't be disturbed.

35
00:02:46.928 --> 00:02:51.517
Finally I got better, to everyone's relief.

36
00:02:51.518 --> 00:02:54.779
I could tell that Little Joe felt terrible.

37
00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:59.914
He'd learned his lesson, and he'd never make those mistakes again.

38
00:02:59.915 --> 00:03:05.564
John stayed angry with Little Joe for a long while.

39
00:03:05.565 --> 00:03:12.310
But as time passed and Joe kept trying to learn, John started to trust him again.

40
00:03:12.311 --> 00:03:17.823
One day the squire needed to send a note to a neighboring estate.

41
00:03:17.824 --> 00:03:23.197
John was out, so the squire told Little Joe to saddle me.

42
00:03:23.198 --> 00:03:26.894
"I know you haven't ridden much," he told Little Joe.

43
00:03:26.895 --> 00:03:33.081
"But Beauty will take care of you. Just ride carefully and you'll be fine."

44
00:03:33.082 --> 00:03:37.433
Little Joe wasn't a skilled rider, but he was gentle and careful.

45
00:03:37.434 --> 00:03:42.855
We delivered the note, then started for home.

46
00:03:42.856 --> 00:03:48.334
On the way we passed a muddy field. A two-horse cart was stuck there.

47
00:03:48.335 --> 00:03:51.855
It was piled high with heavy bricks.

48
00:03:51.856 --> 00:03:57.311
The driver was yelling and whipping his two horses again and again.

49
00:03:57.312 --> 00:04:03.736
Little Joe brought me to a halt. "Stop beating those horses!" he called.

50
00:04:03.737 --> 00:04:06.910
"They can't move the cart with all those bricks in it.

51
00:04:06.911 --> 00:04:09.837
The wheels are stuck in the mud!"

52
00:04:09.838 --> 00:04:14.780
The man ignored him. He lashed the horses once more.

53
00:04:14.781 --> 00:04:20.033
"Please stop!" Little Joe cried. "I'll help you unload some bricks.

54
00:04:20.034 --> 00:04:23.786
Maybe then they can pull out the cart."

55
00:04:23.787 --> 00:04:27.752
"Mind your own business!" the man yelled.

56
00:04:27.753 --> 00:04:33.525
Little Joe turned me around. "Come on, Beauty," he whispered.

57
00:04:33.526 --> 00:04:38.854
"We'd better tell that man's boss what's going on before he kills those horses."

58
00:04:38.855 --> 00:04:42.269
He kicked me into a gallop.

59
00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:47.163
We raced to the brickmaker's house, and Little Joe told him what was happening.

60
00:04:47.164 --> 00:04:49.981
"Thanks for letting me know," the brickmaker said.

61
00:04:49.982 --> 00:04:53.533
"I'll put a stop to it right now."

62
00:04:53.534 --> 00:04:58.315
When we got home, John could see that Little Joe looked angry.

63
00:04:58.316 --> 00:05:05.675
He asked what was wrong, and Little Joe told him the whole story.

64
00:05:05.676 --> 00:05:09.440
"Well done," John said when the boy had finished.

65
00:05:09.441 --> 00:05:12.998
"Many people would have ridden past and not done anything.

66
00:05:12.999 --> 00:05:17.647
But it's everybody's business to put a stop to cruelty when they see it."

67
00:05:17.648 --> 00:05:21.932
Little Joe looked shy and proud of himself at the same time.

68
00:05:21.933 --> 00:05:25.395
After that there was something different about him.

69
00:05:25.396 --> 00:05:29.400
John said it was as if the boy had grown an inch taller that day.

70
00:05:29.401 --> 00:05:34.027
I believe it was true.

